[h2]Hotfix - the Warden of the Spartan Crypt answers you again[/h2]

[b]If you played between 6 August 2026 and today, the only way into the Spartan Crypt was broken.[/b] The [b]Warden of the Spartan Crypt[/b], deep in the Athens catacombs, did not respond when you clicked him - no dialog box, nothing - so the crypt below him could not be reached at all. That entrance shipped on evidence rather than on a confirmed in-game walk, and this update is the correction. Sorry for the dead end.

[list]
[*][b]The Warden opens his dialog.[/b] His travel offer is now registered through the same proven mechanism every other traveller in the mod uses, instead of the one code path that had never been confirmed working in game.
[*][b]He no longer stands on the arrival spot.[/b] He had been placed on exactly the point both Spartan Crypt teleports drop you on, so an arriving player materialised inside him and the click could land on the wrong thing. He has moved a few paces, still right beside the same stairs down.
[*][b]His menu is unchanged:[/b] one option, descend into the Spartan Crypt. Nothing else, by design.
[/list]

Nothing else changed in this update. The database, text and creature archives are byte-for-byte the ones already published; only the level and quest archives moved.

